# RFC-TRADECORE-0026 ChangeQuery Viewport Owner Work

## Background

- COMM correlation: `rfc-tradecore-0026-ptcs-renderer-gate-20260922`.
- Daedalus reports the server-side `ChangeTaQuery` contract is complete, while the owner Renderer currently ignores an `Accepted` response and therefore does not update the local From/To viewport.
- Canonical feedback: `G:\coldfar_py\coldfar-symbolics\doc_new2\RFC\RFC-TRADECORE-0026.PTCS-ChangeQueryViewport.Feedback.md`.

## Goal

Implement the PTCS Renderer owner seam so an accepted query selects a local window from the merged base/reference temporal axis, patch responses merge before selection, stale replies cannot override newer intent, and cache/document/data identity remain authoritative.

## Assumptions

- The Dynamic repo owns renderer/client orchestration only; TradeCore owns query validation and bounded patch production.
- Existing exact package graph and cache semantics from RFC-PTCS-DYNAMIC-0017 must remain intact.
- Performance findings are addressed only where this query path supplies bounded evidence; unrelated host/runtime work remains outside scope.

## Plan

1. Read the canonical feedback and inspect `applyQuery`, query reply types, viewport state, and existing tests.
2. Add focused unit/browser regressions for accepted-in-cache, patch-then-select, invalid/empty range, and latest-query-wins.
3. Implement the smallest owner seam without replacing identities or clearing cache.
4. Run owner tests and the strict browser gate where available; profile only if the new path regresses latency.
5. Synchronize RFC/current-state/WBS/Test/Verification/DevLog, version and publish exact owner packages.
6. Commit/push and reply through the originating COMM correlation with versions, commit and consumer gate instructions.

## Scope

- `PulseTrade.Comm.Spa.Dynamic.Interactive.Client` query orchestration
- Renderer viewport state only where required by the client seam
- focused owner tests, verifier and documentation

## Acceptance

- `Accepted` selects From/To over an already-loaded merged temporal axis.
- Patch reply merges frames before selecting the same requested range.
- Older query replies cannot override the newest query intent.
- Document/data identity and browser cache remain intact.
- Targeted unit/browser tests pass and exact owner packages are published.

## Risks

- Query bounds are UTC and half-open; off-by-one or local-time conversion can select the wrong bar.
- Reply ordering may race with live revisions; generation must gate viewport side effects without dropping valid data patches.
- Selecting zero loaded bars must remain an explicit empty/error presentation rather than silently reverting to the previous viewport.

